<title>USA: Sherwin-Williams sells two businesses.</title>
<headline>Sherwin-Williams sells two businesses.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sherwin-Williams Co. said Tuesday it has completed the sale of two adhesives businesses that were part of the recently acquired Pratt &amp; Lambert United Inc.</p>
<p>The proceeds from the sale of the two businesses, which totalled $58 million, will be used to cut the company's debt, it said.</p>
<p>Pierce &amp; Stevens Corp., a manufacturer of speciality industrial adhesives, was sold to Sovereign Speciality Chemicals Inc.</p>
<p>Miracle Adhesives Corp., a maker of construction adhesives was sold to TACC International Corp.</p>
<p>Sherwin-Williams said the companies had combined annual sales of $80 million.</p>
